{"name":"Luna Pier","hex":"#414d62","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"luna","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A luna moth: a member of species Actias luna.","A lunette: a crescent-shaped receptacle, often glass, for holding the (consecrated) host (the bread of communion) upright when exposed in the monstrance. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A foreman on a plantation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/luna"},{"term":"pier","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A raised platform built from the shore out over water, supported on piles; used to secure, or provide access to shipping; a jetty.","A similar structure, especially at a seaside resort, used to provide entertainment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pier"}],"entries":[{"title":"Luna Pier, Michigan","blocks":[{"text":"Luna Pier is a city in Monroe County in the U.S. state of Michigan. The population was 1,382 at the 2020 census. Previously known as Lakewood, it was established in the early 1900s and incorporated as a city in 1963."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Luna_Pier%2C_MI_Downtown.jpg/330px-Luna_Pier%2C_MI_Downtown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luna_Pier%2C_Michigan","wikidata":"Q2221960"},{"title":"Pier","blocks":[{"text":"A pier is a raised structure that rises above a body of water and usually juts out from its shore, typically supported by piles or pillars, and provides above-water access to offshore areas. Frequent pier uses include fishing, boat docking and access for both passengers and cargo, and oceanside recreation such as swimming. Bridges, buildings, and walkways may all be supported by architectural piers. Their open structure allows tides and currents to flow relatively unhindered, whereas the more solid foundations of a quay or the closely spaced piles of a wharf can act as a breakwater, and are consequently more liable to silting. Piers can range in size and complexity from a simple lightweight wooden structure to major structures extended over 1,600 m (5,200 ft). In American English, a pier may be synonymous with a dock."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Korfu_%28GR%29%2C_Korfu%2C_Altstadt_--_2018_--_1156.jpg/330px-Korfu_%28GR%29%2C_Korfu%2C_Altstadt_--_2018_--_1156.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pier","wikidata":"Q863454"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/26/Lp_cityseal_200px_web.png/120px-Lp_cityseal_200px_web.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/26/Lp_cityseal_200px_web.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/26/Lp_cityseal_200px_web.png/120px-Lp_cityseal_200px_web.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALp_cityseal_200px_web.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Luna_pier.JPG/500px-Luna_pier.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Luna_pier.JPG/1280px-Luna_pier.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Luna_pier.JPG/500px-Luna_pier.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Recreational fishing on Luna Pier","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALuna_pier.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/USPS_Post_Office%2C_Luna_Pier_MI.jpg/500px-USPS_Post_Office%2C_Luna_Pier_MI.jpg?utm_sour